test_set_logic -- eltset and pset union / inter / not (Oct 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_set_logic_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     2 decks, about 1 s
  open logs/summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  eltset / name / union | inter | not / set1 [set2 ...]
  pset   / name / union | inter | not / set1 [set2 ...]
  with 1 to 4 sets, blank- or comma-separated:
    union  members of at least one set
    inter  members of every set
    not    one set: everything else; more: in set1 and in none of the
           others
  Every member of every result is compared with the answer computed by
  the checker, and so is the count LaGriT prints for each set.

THE DECKS

  sl01_eltset   a hex brick of 24 cells; a = cells 1-12, b = 7-18,
                c = odd cells, d = 1, 4, 7, ...; 11 combinations
  sl02_pset     the same brick's 60 vertices; a = 1-30, b = 21-45,
                c = odd, d = 1, 4, 7, ...; the same 11 combinations
  Each result is written to a 0/1 attribute r_<name> and dumped as an
  attribute-only AVS table (sl01_eltset.table, sl02_pset.table).

WHY

  In LaGriT V3.3.4 and earlier, eltset inter and not with three or more
  sets gave wrong results without a message (inter gave an empty set):
  src/eset.f read the running result from the stored set bits instead of
  the work array (inter), and garbled the shift and the and (not). pset
  (src/pset.F) was right. On such a LaGriT, sl01_eltset fails 5 checks
  (i3, i4, ic, n3, n4); with the fix every check passes.

FILES

  run_set_logic_tests.sh   runner (work/, logs/)
  sl01_eltset.lgi          eltset deck
  sl02_pset.lgi            pset deck
  check_set_logic.py       checks, logs/summary.html, logs/table.txt
